{"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Notes are the most common type of MusicXML data. The MusicXML format distinguishes between elements used for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sound information and elements used for notation information (e.g., tie is used for sound, tied for notation)."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Thus grace notes do not have a duration element. Cue notes have a duration element, as do forward elements,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"but no tie elements. Having these two types of information available can make interchange easier, as some"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"programs handle one type of information more readily than the other."}],"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/Kind-swift.struct","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/Notehead-swift.struct","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/NoteheadText-swift.struct"],"title":"Structures"},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/init(id:content:instrument:footnote:level:voice:kind:dot:accidental:timeModification:stem:notehead:noteheadText:staff:beam:notations:lyric:play:listen:xPosition:font:color:printout:printsLeger:dynamics:endDynamics:attack:release:timeOnly:isPizzicato:)"],"title":"Initializers"},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/accidental","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/attack","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/beam","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/color","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/content-swift.property","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/dot","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/dynamics","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/endDynamics","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/font","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/footnote","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/id","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/instrument","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/isPizzicato","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/kind-swift.property","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/level","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/listen","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/lyric","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/notations","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/notehead-swift.property","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/noteheadText-swift.property","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/play","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/printout","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/printsLeger","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/release","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/staff","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/stem","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/timeModification","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/timeOnly","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/voice","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/xPosition"],"title":"Instance Properties"},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Enumerations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/Content-swift.enum"],"title":"Enumerations"},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Default-Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/Equatable-Implementations"],"title":"Default Implementations"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLNote","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The print-leger attribute is used to indicate whether leger lines are printed. Notes without leger lines are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"used to indicate indeterminate high and low notes. By default, it is set to yes. If print-object is set to no,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"print-leger is interpreted to also be set to no if not present. This attribute is ignored for rests."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The dynamics and end-dynamics attributes correspond to MIDI 1.0’s Note On and Note Off velocities,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"respectively. They are expressed in terms of percentages of the default forte value (90 for MIDI 1.0)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The attack and release attributes are used to alter the starting and stopping time of the note from when it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"would otherwise occur based on the flow of durations - information that is specific to a performance. They are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"expressed in terms of divisions, either positive or negative. A note that starts a tie should not have a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"release attribute, and a note that stops a tie should not have an attack attribute. The attack and release"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attributes are independent of each other. The attack attribute only changes the starting time of a note, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the release attribute only changes the stopping time of a note."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If a note is played only particular times through a repeat, the time-only attribute shows which times to play"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the note."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The pizzicato attribute is used when just this note is sounded pizzicato, vs. the pizzicato element which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"changes overall playback between pizzicato and arco."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Maps the MusicXML "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<note>"},{"type":"text","text":" element."}]}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnote"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SQ","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SH","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Music","title":"Music","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMusicItem","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLFullNote","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLRest","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPitch","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAttributes","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDirection","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBarline","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound"]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLNoteV","role":"symbol","title":"MXLNote","roleHeading":"Structure","symbolKind":"struct","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLNote","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLNote","kind":"identifier"}]},"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNote/endDynamics":{"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The Note Off velocity, corresponding to MIDI 1.0’s Note Off velocity, expressed as a percentage of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"default forte value (90 for MIDI 1.0)."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/endDynamics","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnote\/enddynamics","title":"endDynamics","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"endDynamics"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLNonNegativeDecimal","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL21MXLNonNegativeDecimala"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNote/attack":{"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Alters the starting time of the note from when it would otherwise occur, expressed in divisions. A note that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stops a tie should not have an attack attribute."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/attack","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnote\/attack","title":"attack","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"attack"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLDivisions","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLDivisionsV"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/s8CopyableP":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8CopyableP","type":"unresolvable","title":"Swift.Copyable"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDirection":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLDirection"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDirection","title":"MXLDirection","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLDirection"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A direction is a musical indication that is not necessarily attached to a specific note. Two or more may be","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"combined to indicate words followed by the start of a dashed line, the end of a wedge followed by dynamics,","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"etc. For applications where a specific direction is indeed attached to a specific note, the direction element","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"can be associated with the first note element that follows it in score order that is not in a different voice.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldirection"},"doc://IvorMXL/SQ":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SQ","type":"unresolvable","title":"Swift.Equatable"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNote/lyric":{"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The lyrics associated with this note."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/lyric","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnote\/lyric","title":"lyric","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"lyric"},{"kind":"text","text":": ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLLyric","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLLyricV"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNote/init(id:content:instrument:footnote:level:voice:kind:dot:accidental:timeModification:stem:notehead:noteheadText:staff:beam:notations:lyric:play:listen:xPosition:font:color:printout:printsLeger:dynamics:endDynamics:attack:release:timeOnly:isPizzicato:)":{"fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"id"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"content"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Content